(3321349, 454558, 28261, '<td valign="top">Hi Jamie.<br/> <br/>Where this image went wrong mostly was in the sizing.  For many of us here at DPC, if the image is not at least 640px on one side, then a point or two get lost right off the top.  Some people simply (1) anything that isn''t close to that size due to the challenges of trying to view the finer detail.<br/> <br/>This is an image that dutifully fits the challenge and others will give a ten, simply because it fits and the image is crisp and clear.  You have all the technicals down on this image, just not the ''artsy-ness'' of it.<br/> <br/>Imagine if you had been able to get right up close on this hole and shoot an angle that really dropped us into the tree...now, there I would have given some good bonus points.</td>', 'Hi Jamie. Where this image went wrong mostly was in the sizing.  For many of us here at DPC, if the image is not at least 640px on one side, then a point or two get lost right off the top.  Some people simply (1) anything that isn''t close to that size due to the challenges of trying to view the finer detail. This is an image that dutifully fits the challenge and others will give a ten, simply because it fits and the image is crisp and clear.  You have all the technicals down on this image, just not the ''artsy-ness'' of it. Imagine if you had been able to get right up close on this hole and shoot an angle that really dropped us into the tree...now, there I would have given some good bonus points.', '2007-02-03 00:35:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(3322888, 456989, 64176, '<td valign="top">love this one!  and call me a crackhead, but i actually think the halo adds to this shot because it gives the feeling of otherworldy-ness, like this is the door to somewhere otherworldly and ethereal.</td>', 'love this one!  and call me a crackhead, but i actually think the halo adds to this shot because it gives the feeling of otherworldy-ness, like this is the door to somewhere otherworldly and ethereal.', '2007-02-03 13:49:09.000000', NULL, 0),
